WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
[Music]

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.440
[The English Disease]

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:33.020
[Music]

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:42.460
[The English Disease]

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:46.520
[Narrator:] England can claim the sad glory

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.320
that rickets is more widespread there than anywhere else.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.720
It was described there as early as the 17th century

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.740
and has been known as the English Disease ever since.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:16.420
And England used this disease as a weapon against us in the Great War,

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.480
as this extract from an English newspaper proves.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:29.600
[We have tried to stop our enemies from desiring to bring children into the world.]

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:36.860
[Should they reach school age, rickets would ensure

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:43.900
that these half-crippled beings would be mentally deficient.]

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:53.240
This disfiguration of the leg bones is a consequence of rickets.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:13.230
Radiography shows how heavily the bones have been deformed.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:18.080
Thick arms are not always a sign of good health.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:25.300
Here, we observe bone distension due to a lack of vitamin D.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:31.980
On the right side, afflicted arm bones; on the left, healthy ones.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:41.180
Bone development is essential in the development of a child.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.220
Via the bloodstream, the minerals calcium, phosphorus

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:51.350
and vitamin D – here displayed as small triangles --

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:56.230
get into the bone’s growth plate.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:05.470
The building material for bone is a compound of calcium and phosphorus.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:08.870
It is only through vitamin D that calcium is able to bond with phosphorus

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.710
and become calcium phosphate.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:21.960
Hence, vitamin D is an absolute necessity for bone development.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:30.860
Only in this way does bone grow straight and solid.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:37.140
If there is a lack of vitamin D, calcium and phosphorus will not be able to bond.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:42.200
These substances exit the bloodstream, unused.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.080
Development is impaired; bone distensions

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:51.480
and deformations caused by rickets occur as a result.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:04.750
Once bone growth is complete, rickets is no longer curable.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:13.770
The doctor can do no more than to relieve the pain.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:19.020
For women, rickets is particularly disastrous.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:24.820
The normal female pelvis has a round pelvic inlet,

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:32.570
while one affected by rickets is flattened into an oval.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:36.670
A comparison of a normal pelvis

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:40.880
and one affected by rickets clearly shows the deformation.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.830
During birth, the head of the child rotates.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:53.010
This is possible with a normal pelvis; with one flattened due to rickets, in contrast, this cannot occur without difficulty.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:59.950
This nearly always results in difficult childbirth.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:10.690
The first symptoms of rickets: it begins with excessive sweating on the back of the head.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:19.390
General muscular weakness can also be a sign of a disordered mineral metabolism.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:25.220
The hardening of bones in the rib cage

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:32.020
constitutes something which has been called the rickets rosary.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:35.590
A child who isn’t able to stand at the age of one, but who begins to cry painfully

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:42.890
when he or she should be able to stand, is suffering from rickets.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:51.240
Therefore, prevention of the English Disease must start from the earliest stages of infancy.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:58.760
First requirement: the baby has to be breastfed by its mother for as long as possible.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:06.060
For this reason, it is vital that the mother has a healthy lifestyle.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:14.290
Being outside is essential for babies and small children.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.310
This mother is getting it all wrong.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.750
The baby’s head has to be kept out of the sun,

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:26.830
since severe damage could otherwise occur.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:44.540
This is wrong as well, because the baby’s head is still in the sun.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:54.920
Sunbathing must not go on for too long.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:07:02.400
The basic rule is: head in the shade, body in the sunlight.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:15.920
Light, air, and sun: these are our weapons against rickets.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.290
A vitamin-rich diet is also valuable

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:49.440
in the healthy development of children.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:55.420
In plant foods such as salads or vegetables, vitamin D is present

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:59.730
in a preliminary stage, as what is called provitamin.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:10.610
Raw, shredded carrots, spinach and salads are particularly important for the young child.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:19.710
The provitamin ingested with food gets transformed into vitamin D

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:24.760
through the exposure of the human skin to the sun.

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:30.770
A cross-section through the skin: the blood brings the preliminary stage of the vitamin,

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:37.100
which we have called provitamin, to the surface of the skin.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:42.780
When exposed to the rays of the sun on the surface of the skin,

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:46.410
it turns into vitamin D…

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:58.010
…and the bloodstream transports it throughout the whole organism.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:14.930
In months with low sunlight, the danger of falling ill with rickets is particularly high.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:19.520
In winter, the sun alone no longer has the strength to prevent rickets.

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:22.850
For this reason, the counter-measures being taken by the Reich Health Authorities…

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:30.110
…are applied throughout Germany at these times of year.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.560
Every mother is sent to a mothers’ advice center

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:47.780
and the baby receives a thorough examination.

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:30.390
The investigating doctor primarily pays attention to the symptoms of rickets.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.880
To prevent the English Disease, every mother in the Greater German Reich

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:50.460
receives vitamin D in the form of Vigantol.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:59.200
In cases where babies are particularly vulnerable to rickets, for instance premature infants

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:08.840
or twins, treatments with sun lamps are also used.

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:20.490
To prevent rickets, give five drops of Vigantol once a day

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:28.330
with a spoon-full of porridge or other food.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:37.050
National Socialist Germany is ensuring

00:11:37.050 --> 00:12:00.000
that the English Disease will never become a German disease.

